<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — Color Picker dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual + behavioral PARITY reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Pickers/FormColorPicker`
    (source: FormColorPicker.cs + FormColorPicker.Designer.cs, 406 lines). A palette / colour
    selection dialog: a 2-D colour box + a vertical hue slider on the left, two large Day/Night
    colour-preview buttons on the right, a "Select Preset Color" group of 16 preset swatches, a
    lock/unlock toggle that switches between "use a preset" and "save the current colour into a
    preset", and an OK button that closes the dialog. Per AAP §0.3.3 this is a faithful re-platform
    of the currently rendered Windows Forms look — never a redesign: every size, position, font and
    colour below is taken verbatim from FormColorPicker.Designer.cs.

    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    COORDINATION DEPENDENCY (out of this Views/Pickers/ folder's scope — recorded for traceability)
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Per AAP §0.5.1 the WinForms MechanikaDesign colour controls (ColorBox2D + ColorSliderVertical
    from the package `MechanikaDesign.WinForms.UI.ColorPicker`) are REPLACED with the cross-platform
    Avalonia colour controls ColorSpectrum (the 2-D saturation/value plane) + ColorSlider (the
    vertical hue slider). Those controls ship in the **Avalonia.Controls.ColorPicker** NuGet package
    (repo-pinned version 11.3.18), which MUST be referenced by `SourceCode/GPS/AgOpenGPS.csproj`.
    That .csproj is owned by the GPS-root agent (outside this folder), so the PackageReference is
    added there — this comment records the requirement so the dependency stays traceable.

    NAMESPACE NOTE (correction vs. the original instruction): ColorSpectrum and ColorSlider live in
    the CLR namespace `Avalonia.Controls.Primitives` (verified against Avalonia.Controls.ColorPicker
    11.3.18), NOT `Avalonia.Controls`. The package assembly's XmlnsDefinition does map both
    Avalonia.Controls and Avalonia.Controls.Primitives onto the default https://github.com/avaloniaui
    XML namespace, but to keep this markup self-documenting we declare an explicit `xmlns:primitives`
    prefix bound to the correct CLR namespace and use it for the two colour controls.

    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    WIRING CONTRACT — the partner code-behind (FormColorPickerView.axaml.cs) owns ALL behaviour
    ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    This is an IMPERATIVE, code-behind-driven dialog (exactly like the sibling FormYesView /
    FormInputDialogView): there is intentionally NO x:DataType, NO DataContext and NO {Binding}.
    The code-behind resolves every control by x:Name and subscribes every event handler itself with
    `+=` (mirroring the original WinForms Designer, which did `this.btnXX.Click += ...`). Therefore
    NO Click / ColorChanged / IsCheckedChanged attributes are declared in this markup — declaring
    them here would force specific handler signatures to exist and risk double-wiring. The named
    controls below MUST keep these exact names (the code-behind generated x:Name fields depend on
    them): colorBox2D, colorSlider, btnDay, btnNight, groupBoxSelectPresetColor, btn00..btn15,
    chkUse, chkUseImage, btnSave.

    Behaviour reproduced by the code-behind (FormColorPicker.cs):
      * colorBox2D.ColorChanged / colorSlider.ColorChanged keep the box, the slider and the two
        preview buttons in sync and update the public `useThisColor`.
      * btnDay / btnNight are colour-preview swatches: their Background is recoloured to the current
        colour in code-behind (the design-time Background here is cosmetic). Their Text is set at
        runtime from gStr.gsDay / gStr.gsNight (assign Button.Content in code-behind).
      * btn00..btn15 share one handler (Preset_Click). Each carries Tag="00".."15"; the handler
        reads the Tag to know which preset slot it is (replacing the WinForms `Name.Substring(3,2)`
        parse) and either applies the preset (lock / "use" mode) or stores the current colour into
        that slot (unlock / "save" mode).
      * chkUse toggles use/save mode: it swaps chkUseImage between ColorLocked.png and
        ColorUnlocked.png and retitles groupBoxSelectPresetColor; the :checked PaleGreen background
        (WinForms FlatAppearance.CheckedBackColor) is supplied declaratively below.
      * btnSave closes the dialog (WinForms DialogResult.OK).

    SHELL PARITY (FormColorPicker.Designer.cs):
      Text "Color Picker"                  -> Title
      ClientSize 591 x 615                  -> Width / Height (SystemDecorations="None" => client == window)
      BackColor Color.FromArgb(127,127,127) -> Background "#FF7F7F7F" (mid-gray, hard-coded for parity —
                                              theme-independent, like the sibling parity dialogs)
      FormBorderStyle.FixedSingle +
        ControlBox=false + MinimizeBox=false -> SystemDecorations="None" + CanResize="False"
      StartPosition.CenterParent            -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
      ShowInTaskbar=false                   -> ShowInTaskbar="False"
      (not TopMost)                         -> Topmost omitted (defaults False)
      Font Tahoma                           -> FontFamily="Tahoma"

    No System.Windows.Forms, no OpenTK / OpenTK.GLControl, no Win32 types — Avalonia 11.3 markup only.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        xmlns:primitives="using:Avalonia.Controls.Primitives"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.Pickers.FormColorPickerView"
        Title="Color Picker"
        Width="591" Height="615"
        Background="#FF7F7F7F"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        CanResize="False"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <Window.Styles>

        <!-- Colour-preview / preset SWATCH buttons (btnDay, btnNight, btn00..btn15).
             WinForms FlatStyle.Flat/Popup colour buttons render a SOLID fill that IS the swatch, so
             the locally-assigned Background must stay visible in every interaction state (the Fluent
             Button template would otherwise paint a hover/pressed overlay that tints the colour).
             A minimal custom template — one ContentPresenter bound to the templated parent, with no
             state visuals — reproduces this exactly (same proven idiom as the sibling
             Config/ConfigVehicleControl.axaml). Background/Foreground/Content are set per-button
             (design-time) and re-assigned at runtime by the code-behind. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.swatch">
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <ContentPresenter Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                      BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                      BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                      Foreground="{TemplateBinding Foreground}"
                                      FontFamily="{TemplateBinding FontFamily}"
                                      FontSize="{TemplateBinding FontSize}"
                                      FontWeight="{TemplateBinding FontWeight}"
                                      Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                      ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                                      Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                      HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                      VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}" />
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <!-- Flat, transparent, image-only button (btnSave OK glyph). Matches the sibling
             FormYesView OK button: BackColor Transparent + FlatStyle.Flat + BorderSize 0, with
             hover/pressed kept transparent so only the 64x64 glyph shows. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <!-- chkUse — WinForms CheckBox with Appearance=Button, FlatAppearance.BorderSize=0 and
             CheckedBackColor=PaleGreen. As an Avalonia ToggleButton: a flat image button that is
             transparent when unchecked and PaleGreen (#98FB98) when checked. Using the same custom
             template as the swatches, the control's Background drives the fill; the :checked style
             simply flips Background to PaleGreen (the proven ConfigVehicleControl :checked idiom),
             so the checked colour holds across hover/pressed automatically. -->
        <Style Selector="ToggleButton.useToggle">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <ContentPresenter Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                                      BorderBrush="{TemplateBinding BorderBrush}"
                                      BorderThickness="{TemplateBinding BorderThickness}"
                                      Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                      ContentTemplate="{TemplateBinding ContentTemplate}"
                                      Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}"
                                      HorizontalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding HorizontalContentAlignment}"
                                      VerticalContentAlignment="{TemplateBinding VerticalContentAlignment}" />
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="ToggleButton.useToggle:checked">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="PaleGreen" />
        </Style>

    </Window.Styles>

    <!-- FormColorPicker used absolute Location/Size with no anchoring on a fixed 591x615 client,
         so a top-level Canvas reproduces every pixel faithfully (same strategy as the sibling
         Forms->Views ports, e.g. Config/ConfigVehicleControl.axaml). The mid-gray window Background
         shows through as the form face. -->
    <Canvas Width="591" Height="615">

        <!-- colorBox2D — WinForms MechanikaDesign ColorBox2D (ColorMode=Hue) @ (5,6) 360x360.
             Avalonia ColorSpectrum showing the Saturation (X) / Value (Y) plane; hue is the third
             component, driven by colorSlider. ColorChanged is subscribed in the code-behind. -->
        <primitives:ColorSpectrum x:Name="colorBox2D"
                                  Canvas.Left="5" Canvas.Top="6"
                                  Width="360" Height="360"
                                  Shape="Box"
                                  Components="SaturationValue" />

        <!-- colorSlider — WinForms MechanikaDesign ColorSliderVertical (ColorMode=Hue) @ (371,6)
             75x360. Avalonia ColorSlider as a VERTICAL Hue slider (HSVA model; first component =
             Hue), alpha hidden. ColorChanged is subscribed in the code-behind. -->
        <primitives:ColorSlider x:Name="colorSlider"
                                Canvas.Left="371" Canvas.Top="6"
                                Width="75" Height="360"
                                Orientation="Vertical"
                                ColorModel="Hsva"
                                ColorComponent="Component1"
                                IsAlphaVisible="False" />

        <!-- btnDay — colour-preview swatch @ (454,12) 120x162. WinForms FlatStyle.Flat, Tahoma 24pt
             Bold (=32px), default (black) text "Day". Background is recoloured to the selected
             colour by the code-behind; the design-time fill here is cosmetic, and the caption is
             replaced at runtime from gStr.gsDay. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnDay"
                Classes="swatch"
                Canvas.Left="454" Canvas.Top="12"
                Width="120" Height="162"
                Background="#FFCCCCCC"
                Foreground="Black"
                BorderBrush="Gray"
                BorderThickness="1"
                FontFamily="Tahoma"
                FontSize="32"
                FontWeight="Bold"
                HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                Content="Day" />

        <!-- btnNight — colour-preview swatch @ (454,204) 120x162. WinForms FlatStyle.Flat with
             FlatAppearance.BorderColor=White and ForeColor=Window (white) text "Night". Background
             recoloured in code-behind; caption replaced at runtime from gStr.gsNight. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnNight"
                Classes="swatch"
                Canvas.Left="454" Canvas.Top="204"
                Width="120" Height="162"
                Background="#FF333333"
                Foreground="White"
                BorderBrush="White"
                BorderThickness="1"
                FontFamily="Tahoma"
                FontSize="32"
                FontWeight="Bold"
                HorizontalContentAlignment="Center"
                VerticalContentAlignment="Center"
                Content="Night" />

        <!-- groupBoxSelectPresetColor — WinForms GroupBox @ (12,387) 468x216, Tahoma 11.25pt Bold
             (=15px), caption "Select Preset Color". Avalonia has no GroupBox, so this is a titled
             Border + inner Canvas; the caption TextBlock is named so the code-behind can retitle it
             ("Pick New Color and Select Square Below to Save Preset" in unlock/save mode). The 16
             preset swatches keep their GroupBox-relative offsets exactly: x in {10,87,164,241,318,
             395}, y in {30,92,155}. Each swatch carries Tag="00".."15" for the shared Preset_Click;
             the code-behind overwrites all 16 Backgrounds from customColorsList on load, so the
             design-time fills (a neutral grey, plus the two original designer literals on btn01 and
             btn08) are cosmetic only. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="12" Canvas.Top="387"
                Width="468" Height="216"
                BorderBrush="Gray"
                BorderThickness="1"
                CornerRadius="3"
                Background="Transparent">
            <Canvas>
                <TextBlock x:Name="groupBoxSelectPresetColor"
                           Canvas.Left="10" Canvas.Top="2"
                           FontFamily="Tahoma"
                           FontSize="15"
                           FontWeight="Bold"
                           Foreground="Black"
                           Text="Select Preset Color" />

                <!-- Row 0 (y=30) -->
                <Button x:Name="btn00" Classes="swatch" Tag="00" Canvas.Left="10"  Canvas.Top="30" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn01" Classes="swatch" Tag="01" Canvas.Left="87"  Canvas.Top="30" Width="64" Height="47" Background="Coral"     BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn02" Classes="swatch" Tag="02" Canvas.Left="164" Canvas.Top="30" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn03" Classes="swatch" Tag="03" Canvas.Left="241" Canvas.Top="30" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn04" Classes="swatch" Tag="04" Canvas.Left="318" Canvas.Top="30" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn05" Classes="swatch" Tag="05" Canvas.Left="395" Canvas.Top="30" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />

                <!-- Row 1 (y=92) -->
                <Button x:Name="btn06" Classes="swatch" Tag="06" Canvas.Left="10"  Canvas.Top="92" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn07" Classes="swatch" Tag="07" Canvas.Left="87"  Canvas.Top="92" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn08" Classes="swatch" Tag="08" Canvas.Left="164" Canvas.Top="92" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FF99B4D1" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn09" Classes="swatch" Tag="09" Canvas.Left="241" Canvas.Top="92" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn10" Classes="swatch" Tag="10" Canvas.Left="318" Canvas.Top="92" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn11" Classes="swatch" Tag="11" Canvas.Left="395" Canvas.Top="92" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />

                <!-- Row 2 (y=155) -->
                <Button x:Name="btn12" Classes="swatch" Tag="12" Canvas.Left="10"  Canvas.Top="155" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn13" Classes="swatch" Tag="13" Canvas.Left="87"  Canvas.Top="155" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn14" Classes="swatch" Tag="14" Canvas.Left="164" Canvas.Top="155" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
                <Button x:Name="btn15" Classes="swatch" Tag="15" Canvas.Left="241" Canvas.Top="155" Width="64" Height="47" Background="#FFF0F0F0" BorderBrush="Gray" BorderThickness="1" FontFamily="Tahoma" FontSize="32" FontWeight="Bold" />
            </Canvas>
        </Border>

        <!-- chkUse — WinForms CheckBox (Appearance=Button) @ (495,428) 79x73. Flat image toggle; the
             child image is swapped between ColorLocked/ColorUnlocked by the code-behind, and the
             button turns PaleGreen when checked (style above). WinForms ImageAlign=MiddleRight =>
             the glyph is right-aligned within the button. -->
        <ToggleButton x:Name="chkUse"
                      Classes="useToggle"
                      Canvas.Left="495" Canvas.Top="428"
                      Width="79" Height="73"
                      HorizontalContentAlignment="Right"
                      VerticalContentAlignment="Center">
            <Image x:Name="chkUseImage"
                   Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/ColorLocked.png"
                   Width="64" Height="64"
                   Stretch="Uniform" />
        </ToggleButton>

        <!-- btnSave — WinForms OK button @ (503,532) 71x62, BackColor Transparent, FlatStyle.Flat,
             BorderSize 0, Image OK64 (DialogResult.OK). The code-behind closes the dialog. -->
        <Button x:Name="btnSave"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="503" Canvas.Top="532"
                Width="71" Height="62"
                AutomationProperties.Name="OK">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                   Width="64" Height="64"
                   Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
